      "worked": "A line through $(5,9)$ has equation\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny-9&=m(x-5)\\\\\ny&=mx+9-5m.\n\\end{align*}$$\nAt an intersection with the parabola,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2&=mx+9-5m\\\\\nx^2-mx+5m-9&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor tangency, the intersection equation has a repeated root, so $\\Delta=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nm^2-4(5m-9)&=0\\\\\nm^2-20m+36&=0\\\\\n(m-2)(m-18)&=0\\\\\nm&=2\\text{ or }18.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny&=2x+9-5(2)\\\\\ny&=2x-1.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=18$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny&=18x+9-5(18)\\\\\ny&=18x-81.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangents are $y=2x-1$ and $y=18x-81$.",
